---
description: Keep optional addons isolated, composable, and safe with zero or many active packs
alwaysApply: true
---

# Addon architecture

- Core must work with zero active addons.
- Only the runtime loader/middleware may check an addon slug.
- Core screens render named additive slots; never add `if (addons.foo)`.
- Addons may import core contracts/events. Addon A must not import Addon B.
- Addon routes use `addon.active:{slug}`.
- Addon tables, settings, permissions, routes, and page names are namespaced.
- Addon writes belong in services shared by thin Admin/API controllers.
- Addon UI reuses core `Components/Ui` primitives and `theme-*` / `dp-*` tokens; never hardcode palette colors or invent CSS class names.
- Addon migrations live under `addons/{slug}/database/migrations` and run only through `AddonProvisionService`.
- Use manifest `requires` and `conflicts`; reject conflicts before migrations.
- Additive registrations (nav, fields, reports) all render in deterministic `order`.
- Exclusive capabilities must have a core merge policy; never use “last provider wins.”
- Business rules shared across niches (stock tracking, product kind) belong in core.
- Existing core records referenced by addons must remain valid when the addon is removed.
